        "original_id": "9171e10a-5cac-5e55-8345-6848d59d5f12",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Herbie Flowers, Paul McCartney, Elton John, David Bowie, Lou Reed, Melanie, Roy Harper, David Essex, Allan Clarke, Al Kooper, Bryan Ferry, Harry Nilsson, Cat Stevens, Serge Gainsbourg, George Harrison, Ringo Starr\n- Groups: Blue Mink, T. Rex, Sky\n- Albums and Songs: Tumbleweed Connection, Madman Across the Water, Space Oddity, Diamond Dogs, Transformer, Walk on the Wild Side, Candles in the Rain, Bullinamingvase, Rock On, New York City (You're a Woman), The Bride Stripped Bare, Nilsson Schmilsson, Son of Dracula, New Masters, Foreigner, Histoire de Melody Nelson, Give My Regards to Broad Street, Somewhere in England, Gone Troppo, Brainwashed, Stop and Smell the Roses\n- Roles and Topics: Session bass players, soundtrack albums\n\nFacts:\n- Herbie Flowers was a member of Blue Mink, T. Rex, and Sky.\n- Herbie Flowers was one of Britain's best-known session bass players.\n- Herbie Flowers contributed bass to Elton John's albums \"Tumbleweed Connection\" and \"Madman Across the Water.\"\n- Herbie Flowers contributed bass to David Bowie's albums \"Space Oddity\" and \"Diamond Dogs.\"\n- Herbie Flowers contributed bass to Lou Reed's album \"Transformer,\" including the prominent bass line of \"Walk on the Wild Side.\"\n- Herbie Flowers contributed bass to recordings by Melanie, Roy Harper, David Essex, Allan Clarke, Al Kooper, Bryan Ferry, Harry Nilsson, Cat Stevens, Serge Gainsbourg, Paul McCartney, George Harrison, and Ringo Starr.\n- Paul McCartney's \"Give My Regards to Broad Street\" was released in 1984.\n- \"Give My Regards to Broad Street\" was Paul McCartney's fifth studio album.\n- \"Give My Regards to Broad Street\" was also the soundtrack album to Paul McCartney's 1984 film of the same name.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
